[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628551198","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213#issuecomment-2628551198","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213","id":2628551198,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z86crIIe","user":{"login":"ydwu4","id":11565780,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTY1Nzgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11565780?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4","html_url":"https://github.com/ydwu4","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T23:15:22Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T23:15:22Z","body":"I can think of several potential solutions: \n- never re-use buffer for inputs and outputs of while_loop (is this sufficient or overkill)?\n- always clone the inputs for wihle_loop because we cannot statically determine whether body_fn will be run at compilation time. \n- special code-gen the loop body, when we found body_fn is not executed at all (e.g. by maintaining a loop counter), we return a clone of the inputs or we erroring out (this is how custom ops handle it). The downside of this is that the clone cannot be fused with any operators.\n\nWondering what're your thoughts? @eellison @Chillee @desertfire @zou3519 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628551198/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628561318","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213#issuecomment-2628561318","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213","id":2628561318,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z86crKmm","user":{"login":"zou3519","id":5652049,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTIwNDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5652049?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519","html_url":"https://github.com/zou3519","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zou3519/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T23:26:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T23:27:11Z","body":"I don't think the clone in 2 can be fused either. The clone in 2 cannot be fused because if it does get fused away, then we have the same problem all over again.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628561318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628566343","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213#issuecomment-2628566343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213","id":2628566343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z86crL1H","user":{"login":"ydwu4","id":11565780,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTY1Nzgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11565780?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4","html_url":"https://github.com/ydwu4","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydwu4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-31T23:32:11Z","updated_at":"2025-01-31T23:32:11Z","body":"> The clone in 2 cannot be fused because if it does get fused away, then we have the same problem all over again.\n\nyeah, while_loop need to have dedicated memory for the carries.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628566343/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628605793","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213#issuecomment-2628605793","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213","id":2628605793,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z86crVdh","user":{"login":"Chillee","id":6355099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTUwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6355099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee","html_url":"https://github.com/Chillee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Chillee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T00:16:46Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T00:17:53Z","body":"I think we should special codegen the loop body so that we clone the inputs if there are no iterations. \n\nIf you imagine the world with static memory allocations, the while_loop should always place its output in a particular memory location. If we don't run any iterations we should still move the data to the correct memory location.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2628605793/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4446155359","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213#issuecomment-4446155359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/146213","id":4446155359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z88AAAABCQLyXw","user":{"login":"aorenste","id":19294870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0ODcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste","html_url":"https://github.com/aorenste","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aorenste/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T00:02:51Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T00:02:51Z","body":"Reproduces on PyTorch 2.7; first fixed in a release between 2.7 and 2.13.0.dev20260510+cpu.\n\nVersions tested:\n\n| PyTorch | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| 2.7 | Reproduces (`AssertionError: BUG: while_loop compiled output differs from eager due to buffer…`) |\n| 2.13.0.dev20260510+cpu | Passes |\n\nClosing as completed.\n\n_(Automated bisection — `bisect_version`.)_","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/4446155359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]